  "trace": [
    "Catalog Alacritty is a terminal app with cliBinDir Contents/MacOS; Z_s marks it available from system or user Applications bundle directories.",
    "ICi renders P9 for a nonarchived local workspace and passes userVisiblePath as pathToOpen, openWithinPath and directoryFallbackPath with type workspace.",
    "P9 selects catalog apps passing Gce local eligibility and dispatches selected app to uD with the same workspace path/boundary.",
    "In uD for that local workspace, v/h4i/rvs clamp the parent directory to the workspace boundary, keeping the selected workspace as D.",
    "The alacritty branch first invokes alacritty msg create-window --working-directory D. On code 0 it activates with open -a Alacritty. Otherwise it invokes open -na Alacritty --args --working-directory D and checks the fallback exit code.",
    "OGe appends /Applications/Alacritty.app/Contents/MacOS and $HOME/Applications/Alacritty.app/Contents/MacOS after existing PATH for the CLI request.",
    "Current main offers Alacritty but run_macos_open has only WezTerm/Xcode special handling. Folder launches use open -a Alacritty D without the IPC create-window/cwd fallback sequence. commands.rs adds a bundle PATH only for wezterm."
  ],
